OSVplat patch for LichtFeld-Studio 3067e9e0 (applied by scripts/setup_lichtfeld.sh).
Intended for upstream; drop it once LichtFeld has both features.

1. --save-steps: project (.licht) snapshot iterations as a comma list, like
   --eval-steps (same parser, scaled by --steps-scaler). Until now save_steps
   (default 7000,30000) could only be set through --config, which replaces the
   whole optimisation parameter set.
2. SIGUSR1 in plain headless mode requests a project snapshot without stopping
   training (Trainer::request_project_save, the path --tcp-connection's
   save_project uses), for spot-reclaim notices. Wired for the span of train()
   only; outside it the request is logged and dropped.

Measured for OSVplat #10: the resolved parameters with --save-steps equal those
with a --config dump carrying save_steps; see the issue for timings.

